{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>ויאמר</b> — It is written מן מאכלכם, and this is the bread and the bag, ומשתיכם is plural language, which the king drinks in the days of summer and winter; from it they too drink." "<b>פניכם זועפים</b> — like the faces of angry men." "<b>כגילכם</b> — It has no parallel in Scripture, only in the words of our early sages: בן גילו." "<b>וחיבתם</b> — From the same root as חבולתו; חוב and these are two binyanim and their root, like קם with קים, the words of these Purim."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:53.614721157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}